## What Is BPMN?

BPMN stands for **Business Process Model and Notation**. It is an open international standard — maintained by the Object Management Group (OMG) — for drawing business process diagrams in a way that is consistent, structured, and readable across teams and tools.

Think of it as a shared visual language for describing *how work gets done*. Instead of each team inventing their own flowchart conventions, BPMN gives everyone a common grammar: agreed shapes, symbols, and rules that mean the same thing regardless of who drew the diagram or which tool they used to open it.

The current version, **BPMN 2.0**, has been the standard since 2011 and is widely adopted across industries — from banking to healthcare to manufacturing.

